 `<Popover>`, handling open state and positioning automatically.\nBased on RAC `DialogTrigger`. To anchor a popover to an element it doesn't wrap, pass `triggerRef` instead."},"848":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-12","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#default","content":"Use it with `<PopoverTrigger>`, which wraps both the popover content and an interactive trigger element (for example, a `Button`)."},"849":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-13","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#custom-anchor","content":"To position a popover relative to a different element than its trigger, use the `triggerRef` and `isOpen` props instead of `<PopoverTrigger>`. `onOpenChange` is called when the user opens or closes the popover."},"850":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-14","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#title-and-close-button","content":"Add a `Heading slot=\"title\"` and a `CloseButton` for a titled, dismissible popover. The heading\nalso gives the dialog its accessible name."},"851":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-15","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#keyboard","content":"Key"},"852":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-16","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#keyboard","content":"Action"},"853":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-17","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#keyboard","content":"`Enter/Space`"},"854":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-18","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#keyboard","content":"Opens the popover from its trigger"},"855":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-19","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#keyboard","content":"`Escape`"},"856":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-20","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#keyboard","content":"Closes the popover"},"857":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-21","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#aria","content":"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"},"858":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-22","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#aria","content":"A `Heading slot=\"title\"` labels the dialog via `aria-labelledby`. Without one, a popover inside\na `PopoverTrigger` falls back to being labelled by its trigger; standing alone with\n`triggerRef` it needs an explicit `aria-label`"},"859":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-23","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#best-practices","content":"Pass an `aria-label` when anchoring with `triggerRef` instead of wrapping a `PopoverTrigger`,\nsince there is no trigger to borrow the name from."},"860":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-24","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#best-practices","content":"Popover width is determined by its content, and it's recommended to keep it under 400px."},"861":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-25","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#props","content":"The `Popover` component accepts the following props:"},"862":{"id":"/docs/components/popover-26","page_id":"/docs/components/popover","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/popover#props","content":"The `PopoverTrigger` component accepts the following props:"},"863":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"page","content":"Pressable","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable"},"864":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-0","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable","content":"A wrapperless interaction primitive that adds accessible press behavior to a single child element."},"865":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-1","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#features","content":"Features"},"866":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-2","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#installation","content":"Installation"},"867":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-3","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#examples","content":"Examples"},"868":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-4","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#default","content":"Default"},"869":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-5","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#customization","content":"Customization"},"870":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-6","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"871":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-7","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"872":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-8","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"873":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-9","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/pressable#props","content":"Props"},"874":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-10","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#features","content":"Adds accessible press behavior to an existing visual component."},"875":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-11","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#features","content":"Applies interaction states directly to the child without adding a wrapper element."},"876":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-12","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#features","content":"Supports pointer, touch, and keyboard interactions through React Aria."},"877":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-13","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#features","content":"Preserves the child's layout, shape, and base visual styling while adding state feedback."},"878":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-14","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#default","content":"Add accessible press behavior to an existing visual component without adding a wrapper element.\nThe surface supports pointer, touch, and keyboard activation."},"879":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-15","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#customization","content":"Use `Pressable` when an existing visual component or layout surface needs press behavior while keeping its own DOM element, layout, and styles. The child must be a single element that forwards its ref and accepts the DOM, ARIA, and event props supplied by React Aria."},"880":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-16","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#customization","content":"Use `Button` when you need a standard button control with button-specific sizing, layout, and visual variants."},"881":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-17","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#customization","content":"Pass `onPress` for the action instead of wiring separate pointer and keyboard handlers:"},"882":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-18","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#accessibility","content":"`Pressable` accepts the React Aria press props, including `onPress`, `onPressStart`, `onPressEnd`, `onPressUp`, and `onPressChange`."},"883":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-19","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#accessibility","content":"Use a semantic interactive element when possible. For a non-semantic child such as `Avatar` or `Box`, provide an appropriate interactive role and an accessible name. Pressable makes the child focusable when the required props are forwarded."},"884":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-20","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#accessibility","content":"Do not add `role=\"button\"` to a native `<button>` or `<a>` unless you intentionally need to change its semantics. Use a dedicated semantic component such as `Button`, `LinkButton`, `Menu`, or `ToggleButton` when that control's meaning is known."},"885":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-21","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#best-practices","content":"Prefer a native interactive element or a semantic Antares component when the interaction meaning is known."},"886":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-22","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#best-practices","content":"Avoid nesting interactive elements inside the child passed to `Pressable`."},"887":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-23","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#best-practices","content":"`Pressable` automatically applies React Aria state attributes such as `[data-hovered]`, `[data-pressed]`, `[data-focus-visible]`, and `[data-disabled]` to the child. Ensure the child component styles these states appropriately if it overrides the default `Pressable` styles."},"888":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-24","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#troubleshooting","content":"If React Aria warns that the child must be focusable, ensure it is a single element that forwards its ref, `tabIndex`, DOM props, and ARIA attributes."},"889":{"id":"/docs/components/pressable-25","page_id":"/docs/components/pressable","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pressable#troubleshooting","content":"If `onPress` does not fire, confirm that the child forwards event handlers and is not disabled by another component."},"890":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","type":"page","content":"ProgressBar","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-bar"},"891":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-0","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-bar","content":"A progress bar shows determinate progress of an operation over time"},"892":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-1","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#installation","content":"Installation"},"893":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-2","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#examples","content":"Examples"},"894":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-3","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#default","content":"Default"},"895":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-4","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"896":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-5","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#statuses","content":"Statuses"},"897":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-6","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"898":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-7","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#aria-support","content":"ARIA Support"},"899":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-8","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#props","content":"Props"},"900":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-9","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#default","content":"A determinate progress bar with a label and helper text."},"901":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-10","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#sizes","content":"Three track heights are available: `xs` (6px), `sm` (12px), and `md` (24px)."},"902":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-11","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#statuses","content":"Use the `status` prop to communicate intent: `default`, `success`, `warning`, or `critical`. Pair with `helperText` to provide additional context."},"903":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-12","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#aria-support","content":"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"},"904":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-13","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#aria-support","content":"`aria-valuenow` reflects the current value"},"905":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-14","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#aria-support","content":"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"},"906":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-15","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#aria-support","content":"`aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`)"},"907":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-bar-16","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-bar#aria-support","content":"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"},"908":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"page","content":"ProgressSteps","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps"},"909":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-0","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps","content":"A multi-step progress indicator for wizard and onboarding flows."},"910":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-1","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#features","content":"Features"},"911":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-2","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#installation","content":"Installation"},"912":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-3","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#examples","content":"Examples"},"913":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-4","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#default","content":"Default"},"914":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-5","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#not-started","content":"Not started"},"915":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-6","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#vertical","content":"Vertical"},"916":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-7","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#interactive","content":"Interactive"},"917":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-8","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#disabled","content":"Disabled"},"918":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-9","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#hide-step-numbers","content":"Hide Step Numbers"},"919":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-10","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#customization","content":"Customization"},"920":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-11","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"921":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-12","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"922":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-13","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"923":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-14","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#props","content":"Props"},"924":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-15","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#features","content":"Horizontal and vertical orientations"},"925":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-16","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#features","content":"Four completion statuses (`none`, `partial`, `complete`, `error`) with status icons"},"926":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-17","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#features","content":"Timeline (past / current / future) derived from a single `currentStep` prop"},"927":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-18","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#features","content":"Auto-generated step numbers (opt out with `hideStepNumbers`)"},"928":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-19","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#features","content":"Interactive (navigable) and inert (display-only) steps"},"929":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-20","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#features","content":"Title truncation and RTL support"},"930":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-21","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#features","content":"Rendered as a `<nav>` landmark with an ordered list for assistive technology"},"931":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-22","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#default","content":"A horizontal stepper. `currentStep` marks the active step; earlier steps are `past`, later are `future`. Each `status` sets the step's icon, and an `error` step turns its accent bar red."},"932":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-23","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#not-started","content":"No `currentStep`: the flow hasn't started, so every step is `future` and none is marked current."},"933":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-24","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#vertical","content":"Vertical orientation: accent bar on the leading edge, steps stacked in a column."},"934":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-25","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#interactive","content":"Interactive steps: each `onPress` navigates the wizard by updating `currentStep`."},"935":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-26","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#disabled","content":"A disabled interactive step is muted, not focusable, and cannot be activated."},"936":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-27","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#hide-step-numbers","content":"Step numbers are shown by default; `hideStepNumbers` omits the \"N. \" prefix."},"937":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-28","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#customization","content":"Step numbers (`\"N. \"`) are prepended automatically — keep them where possible, as user testing shows people recognize the component better with them. Set `hideStepNumbers` to omit them."},"938":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-29","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#customization","content":"`orientation` switches between `horizontal` (accent bar on top) and `vertical` (accent bar on the leading edge)."},"939":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-30","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#customization","content":"`currentStep` is the single source of truth for the timeline. Omit it for a not-yet-started flow where every step is `future`; pass the step count for a fully completed flow where every step is `past`."},"940":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-31","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#customization","content":"`status` is independent of timeline and only controls the status icon and (for `error`) the accent bar color."},"941":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-32","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#customization","content":"Pass `className` to the container or an individual step to extend the styles."},"942":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-33","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#accessibility","content":"The container renders a `<nav>` landmark; set `aria-label` to name it (defaults to `\"Progress\"`)."},"943":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-34","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#accessibility","content":"Steps are an ordered list (`<ol>`/`<li>`) so assistive technology conveys position and count."},"944":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-35","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#accessibility","content":"The current step is marked with `aria-current=\"step\"`."},"945":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-36","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#accessibility","content":"Interactive steps are real buttons: focusable in the natural **Tab** order and activated with **Enter** or **Space**. Status icons are decorative (`aria-hidden`)."},"946":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-37","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#accessibility","content":"Focus is shown with a visible outline; disabled steps use `0.4` opacity and are not focusable."},"947":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-38","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#best-practices","content":"Drive the timeline from `currentStep` rather than styling individual steps."},"948":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-39","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#best-practices","content":"Provide `onPress` only for steps a user can actually navigate to; leave it off for display-only steps."},"949":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-40","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#best-practices","content":"Keep titles short — they truncate with an ellipsis when space is tight."},"950":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-41","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#best-practices","content":"Always give the container an `aria-label` that describes the flow (e.g. `\"Checkout progress\"`)."},"951":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-42","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#troubleshooting","content":"**No step is highlighted:** `currentStep` is omitted, negative, or out of range. Set it to the active step's 0-based index."},"952":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-43","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#troubleshooting","content":"**A step isn't clickable:** it has no `onPress`, so it's inert by design. Add `onPress` to make it interactive."},"953":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-44","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#troubleshooting","content":"**Titles overflow:** that's expected — titles truncate. Shorten the title."},"954":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-45","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#props","content":"The `ProgressSteps` component has the following props:"},"955":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-steps-46","page_id":"/docs/components/progress-steps","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress-steps#props","content":"The `ProgressStep` component has the following props:"},"956":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"page","content":"RangeField","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field"},"957":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-0","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field","content":"RangeField lets users select one numeric value or a related set of values on a bounded scale."},"958":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-1","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#features","content":"Features"},"959":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-2","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#installation","content":"Installation"},"960":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-3","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#examples","content":"Examples"},"961":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-4","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#default","content":"Default"},"962":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-5","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#controlled","content":"Controlled"},"963":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-6","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#disabled","content":"Disabled"},"964":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-7","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#labels","content":"Labels"},"965":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-8","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#value-display","content":"Value Display"},"966":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-9","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#markers","content":"Markers"},"967":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-10","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#range","content":"Range"},"968":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-11","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"969":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-12","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"Accessible names"},"970":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-13","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Keyboard interaction"},"971":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-14","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"972":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-15","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#props","content":"Props"},"973":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-16","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"974":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-17","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#a-thumb-is-missing-a-label-or-form-value","content":"A thumb is missing a label or form value"},"975":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-18","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#typescript-reports-the-wrong-callback-value-type","content":"TypeScript reports the wrong callback value type"},"976":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-19","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-controlled-thumbs-do-not-move","content":"The controlled thumbs do not move"},"977":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-20","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#values-snap-unexpectedly","content":"Values snap unexpectedly"},"978":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-21","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-final-marker-is-missing","content":"The final marker is missing"},"979":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-22","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#markers-are-crowded-or-rendering-is-slow","content":"Markers are crowded or rendering is slow"},"980":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-23","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-value-or-endpoint-labels-are-blank","content":"The value or endpoint labels are blank"},"981":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-24","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#negative-values-do-not-behave-as-expected","content":"Negative values do not behave as expected"},"982":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-25","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-range-configuration-is-invalid","content":"The range configuration is invalid"},"983":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-26","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#features","content":"Select one value or render one thumb for each value in an array"},"984":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-27","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#features","content":"Supports controlled and uncontrolled values with typed change callbacks"},"985":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-28","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#features","content":"Provides localized value output, endpoint labels, descriptions, and markers"},"986":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-29","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#features","content":"Integrates with native forms, keyboard, pointer, and touch interaction through React Aria"},"987":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-30","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#default","content":"Minimal usage with a single value and min/max bounds."},"988":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-31","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#controlled","content":"Use `onChange` for immediate updates and `onChangeEnd` for work that should run after interaction finishes."},"989":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-32","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#disabled","content":"Use `isDisabled` when the value is visible but unavailable for interaction."},"990":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-33","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#labels","content":"Combine an input label, value label, range labels, and helper text when users need additional context."},"991":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-34","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#value-display","content":"Use `valueLabel` to show formatted values, static context, or output derived from the current slider state."},"992":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-35","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#markers","content":"Use `markers` to expose a manageable set of discrete steps for a single value."},"993":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-36","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#range","content":"Pass a `number[]` to render a range with two thumbs and step markers."},"994":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-37","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"For a single value, prefer a visible `label`; use `aria-label` only when equivalent visible context already exists."},"995":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-38","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"For an array, provide one descriptive `thumbLabels` entry for every value. Entries are matched by index, so keep them aligned when values are added, removed, or reordered. Describe each thumb's purpose, such as `Lower warning threshold`, rather than its current number."},"996":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-39","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"`thumbNames` configures native form field names and does not provide accessible labels. Likewise, `valueLabel`, `minLabel`, and `maxLabel` are visual context rather than substitutes for accessible naming."},"997":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-40","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Each thumb follows the React Aria slider keyboard model:"},"998":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-41","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Tab and Shift+Tab move among thumbs and surrounding controls."},"999":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-42","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Arrow Right and Arrow Up increase the focused value by `step`."},"1000":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-43","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Arrow Left and Arrow Down decrease the focused value by `step`."},"1001":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-44","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Home and End move the focused thumb to its permitted bounds."},"1002":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-45","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Page Up and Page Down make larger changes."},"1003":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-46","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Directional behavior follows the user's locale where appropriate. Pointer, touch, and keyboard interaction all use the same scale and constraints."},"1004":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-47","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Markers are decorative and hidden from the accessibility tree. Ensure the field label, thumb labels, bounds, step, and formatted values communicate all required information without relying on marker appearance."},"1005":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-48","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use an array only when every entry has a clear, independently adjustable meaning."},"1006":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-49","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Keep `value`, `thumbLabels`, and `thumbNames` aligned by index."},"1007":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-50","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use thumb labels that explain purpose instead of repeating the current number."},"1008":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-51","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Keep array values in a stable semantic order. If crossing or reordering thumbs would make their meaning ambiguous, enforce the appropriate ordering in product state."},"1009":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-52","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Avoid large value arrays. Every entry creates another focusable control, which increases keyboard effort and cognitive load."},"1010":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-53","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Set meaningful `minValue`, `maxValue`, and `step` values. The scale should match the precision users actually need."},"1011":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-54","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use markers only when there are few enough steps to scan. Tiny steps across a large range can create an excessive number of DOM elements."},"1012":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-55","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `formatOptions` for currency, percentages, measurements, and other locale-sensitive units so values display and announce their meaning."},"1013":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-56","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `description` for persistent guidance and `isRequired` when a value is required."},"1014":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-57","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `isDisabled` when the value should remain visible but unavailable for interaction."},"1015":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-58","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `onChange` for lightweight immediate feedback and `onChangeEnd` for expensive requests, filtering, or calculations."},"1016":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-59","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use a text-entry control when exact numeric input is essential. A track is best for exploring or adjusting values within known bounds."},"1017":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-60","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#a-thumb-is-missing-a-label-or-form-value","content":"Check the same index in `thumbLabels` and `thumbNames`. Each array entry renders a thumb, and its accessible label and form name are read from the corresponding positions. A form name does not replace an accessible label."},"1018":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-61","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#typescript-reports-the-wrong-callback-value-type","content":"Keep the controlled or default value and callback signatures consistent. When inference is unavailable, provide the generic explicitly: `<RangeField<number>>` for a scalar or `<RangeField<number[]>>` for an array."},"1019":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-62","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-controlled-thumbs-do-not-move","content":"The `value` prop is the source of truth. Update the scalar or array in `onChange` without changing its intended shape. For arrays, return a new array so application state observes the update."},"1020":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-63","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#values-snap-unexpectedly","content":"Verify that `step` represents the intended interval from `minValue`. Every thumb snaps to valid positions on the same configured scale."},"1021":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-64","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-final-marker-is-missing","content":"Markers begin at `minValue` and appear at complete step positions. `maxValue` receives a marker only when the range is evenly divisible by `step`."},"1022":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-65","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#markers-are-crowded-or-rendering-is-slow","content":"Increase `step` or omit `markers`. Larg